<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akkad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akkad was the capital city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>, founded or developed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a> in the twenty-fourth century BCE. Its exact location in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> has never been identified. The city gave its name to the empire, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-language">Akkadian language</a> and the region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>.</p></div>
